Phase 10.5 step 1 : pure host-side builders for the Synaptics bootstrap
exchange (0x93 DoPairBasic). Mirrors python/verimark/bootstrap.py
byte-for-byte. NO crypto, NO transport in this commit — those are
gated behind step 2 once the data layouts are verified against the
python reference at the byte level.

New module bootstrap.{h,c} exposes :

- verimark_bootstrap_build_p256_params_blob   — 420 B BCRYPT_ECC blob
  (NIST P-256 constants encoded in the Windows-driver expected
  little-endian layout, no sensor-specific data)
- verimark_bootstrap_build_storage_cert       — 400 B client_cert in
  the format the sensor stores (sub1 tag 1)
- verimark_bootstrap_build_wire_cert          — 400 B client_cert
  with DER signature in the format the 0x93 OUT expects
- verimark_bootstrap_parse_pair_response      — split the 802 B
  0x93 IN reply into header + storage_cert + server_cert
- verimark_bootstrap_serialize_sub1           — 1284 B TLV blob
  (tags 2, 1, 4, 3, 0) ready for /var/lib/fprint/verimark/sub1.bin

Test suite : 15/15 tests green, bit-exact against python reference
vectors (SHA-256 of every output matches the python harness output).

Drafted with AI assistance.
